@nsobid-BBA3811191DE71D9B55E53F918AE5DC1

# ARMS 5.5.1 - Double Buffering

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces a two-texture swapchain.
//
// The application builds its sead::GameFrameworkNx::CreateArg with
// isTripleBuffer (+0x1D) set, which initializeGraphicsSystem hands to
// sead::DisplayBufferNvn::setTripleBuffer; that sets the NVN window
// texture count to 3. Passing false instead selects 2, so the CPU can run
// at most one frame ahead of scanout, cutting a frame of input latency.

@enabled
00C6C060 01008052   // MOV W1,#0 for setTripleBuffer (was LDRB W1,[X19,#0xBD])
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against ARMS 5.5.1 (Cstm/Lp + gsys/agl +
// sead, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was located
// by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
